<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/consultation.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/consultation-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/consultation.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Questions answered</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Answers</p><h1>Insurance Appraisal Questions, Answered for Delaware</h1><p class="lede">Plain answers to the questions we hear most, grouped by topic: the process, Delaware specifics, costs, timing and working with us.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/start-your-review/">Free claim review</a></div></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><nav class="toc" aria-label="FAQ topics"><p class="local-k">Jump to a topic</p><ul><li><a href="#faq-0">Appraisal basics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-1">Delaware specifics</a></li><li><a href="#faq-2">Costs &amp; fees</a></li><li><a href="#faq-3">Timing &amp; deadlines</a></li><li><a href="#faq-4">Working with us</a></li></ul></nav><h2 id="faq-0">Appraisal basics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>What is insurance appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It’s a process written into most property policies for resolving disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side picks an appraiser, the appraisers pick an umpire, and any two of the three can sign a binding award on the amount.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is appraisal the same as arbitration?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>They’re similar but not identical. Appraisal is limited to the amount of loss, while arbitration can address broader issues. How courts treat each can differ, so ask an attorney if the distinction matters to your case.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does appraisal decide coverage?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Appraisal sets the amount of loss. Whether something is covered is a separate question for the insurer, the Department of Insurance or the courts.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can the insurance company demand appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Either party can invoke appraisal under most policies, and the process works the same way regardless of who demands it.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-1">Delaware specifics</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who regulates insurance in Delaware?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The Delaware Department of Insurance, led by an elected Insurance Commissioner. The department handles consumer complaints and enforces the state’s insurance laws, including unfair claim practices rules.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does Delaware have a FAIR plan?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Delaware’s FAIR plan, the Insurance Placement Facility of Delaware, provides basic property coverage for owners who can’t find it in the regular market. Its policies have their own terms, so check whether yours includes an appraisal provision.</p></div></details><details><summary>What does Delaware law say about bad faith?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Delaware regulates unfair claim settlement practices through Title 18 of the Delaware Code, enforced by the Department of Insurance, and Delaware courts have recognized bad-faith claims against insurers in some circumstances. These are legal questions; appraisal doesn’t address them, so talk to a Delaware attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>How many counties does Delaware have?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Three: New Castle, Kent and Sussex — the fewest of any state. We work in all three.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is flood covered by my homeowners policy?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually not. Flood from storm surge, tides or rising creeks is typically covered by a separate NFIP or private flood policy.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-2">Costs &amp; fees</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Who pays for appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Each side pays its own appraiser, and the umpire’s fee is usually split equally. Check your policy for the exact terms.</p></div></details><details><summary>How do appraisers charge?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Fees may be flat, hourly or a percentage of the increase. We put our fee in writing before any work starts.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is it worth it for a small gap?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Often not. If the gap is only a few thousand dollars, a documented supplement request may resolve it faster and cheaper.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-3">Timing &amp; deadlines</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How long does appraisal take?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many residential claims resolve within six to twelve weeks of both appraisers being named. Complex claims take longer.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is there a deadline to invoke appraisal?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Some policies include one, and other deadlines (such as suit limitations) still run. Read your policy and talk to an attorney if a deadline is close.</p></div></details><details><summary>When should I involve an attorney?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>If coverage is denied, a deadline is approaching, the insurer alleges fraud, or you believe the insurer acted in bad faith.</p></div></details></div><h2 id="faq-4">Working with us</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Do you serve all of Delaware?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes, every community in New Castle, Kent and Sussex counties, from Claymont to Fenwick Island.</p></div></details><details><summary>Are you a public adjuster?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. We work as appraisers, estimators and umpires. We don’t negotiate claims outside appraisal, and we don’t give legal advice.</p></div></details><details><summary>What should I send for a free review?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>The carrier’s full estimate, your declarations page, any letters from the insurer, your photos and any contractor estimates.</p></div></details></div></article><aside class="sidebar"><div class="sticky"><div class="side-box side-call"><h2 class="side-h">Talk it through, free</h2><p>A short call tells you whether appraisal fits your claim — and if it doesn’t, what will.</p><a class="side-tel" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-coral" href="/start-your-review/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri 8am–6pm ET</small></div><div class="side-box"><h2 class="side-h">Resources</h2><ul class="side-list"><li><a href="/how-the-appraisal-panel-works/">Appraisal roadmap<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/delaware-appraisal-faq/" aria-current="page">Questions answered<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/claim-terms-explained/">Claim terms<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-journal/">Appraisal journal<svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div><section class="cta-band"><div class="wrap cta-in rv"><div><h2>Didn’t see your question?</h2><p>Call or email — we’re happy to talk it through.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/start-your-review/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
